From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gloat <4354076+gloat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:59:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] window rules: per-window open and close animations
 (window-open, window-close)

A window rule can carry its own window-open / window-close block, same syntax as in animations {},
replacing the global animation for matching windows: duration, curve or spring, off, and
custom-shader. Without a custom-shader the rule uses niri's built-in animation. Rule shaders are
compiled on first use, once per distinct source, and cached for the session (ProgramType::Rule).
